### Options to Resolve

Since the problem is tied to Spring AI’s vector search, here are your options:

#### Option 1: Manual Vector Search with `MongoTemplate`

Bypass Spring AI’s `MongoDBAtlasVectorStore` and implement the similarity search directly using `MongoTemplate` with Atlas’s `$vectorSearch` operator.

```java
import org.springframework.data.mongodb.core.MongoTemplate;
import org.springframework.data.mongodb.core.aggregation.Aggregation;
import org.springframework.data.mongodb.core.aggregation.AggregationOperation;
import org.springframework.ai.document.Document;
import org.springframework.ai.embedding.EmbeddingModel;
import java.util.List;
import java.util.stream.Collectors;

public class ManualVectorSearch {

    private final MongoTemplate mongoTemplate;
    private final EmbeddingModel embeddingModel;

    public ManualVectorSearch(MongoTemplate mongoTemplate, EmbeddingModel embeddingModel) {
        this.mongoTemplate = mongoTemplate;
        this.embeddingModel = embeddingModel;
    }

    public List<Document> similaritySearch(String query, int topK, double similarityThreshold) {
        // Generate embedding for the query
        float[] queryEmbedding = embeddingModel.embed(query);

        // Build the $vectorSearch aggregation pipeline
        AggregationOperation vectorSearch = Aggregation.stage(new com.mongodb.BasicDBObject("$vectorSearch", 
            new com.mongodb.BasicDBObject()
                .append("index", "vector_index")
                .append("path", "embedding")
                .append("queryVector", queryEmbedding)
                .append("numCandidates", topK * 10) // Adjust for better results
                .append("limit", topK)
        ));

        AggregationOperation project = Aggregation.stage(new com.mongodb.BasicDBObject("$project", 
            new com.mongodb.BasicDBObject()
                .append("content", 1)
                .append("metadata", 1)
                .append("score", new com.mongodb.BasicDBObject("$meta", "vectorSearchScore"))
        ));

        Aggregation aggregation = Aggregation.newAggregation(vectorSearch, project);

        // Execute the aggregation
        List<com.mongodb.DBObject> results = mongoTemplate.aggregate(aggregation, "default_vector_collection", com.mongodb.DBObject.class)
                .getMappedResults();

        // Convert to Spring AI Document
        return results.stream()
                .filter(result -> (double) result.get("score") >= similarityThreshold)
                .map(result -> new Document(
                        (String) result.get("content"),
                        (java.util.Map<String, Object>) result.get("metadata"),
                        (float) ((double) result.get("score"))
                ))
                .collect(Collectors.toList());
    }
}
```

- **Usage**:
  ```java
  @Autowired
  private MongoTemplate mongoTemplate;

  @Autowired
  private EmbeddingModel embeddingModel;

  public List<Document> retrieve(String query) {
      ManualVectorSearch search = new ManualVectorSearch(mongoTemplate, embeddingModel);
      return search.similaritySearch(query, 5, 0.7);
  }
  ```

- **Why It Works**:
  - Uses your proven `MongoTemplate` directly, avoiding Spring AI’s vector store logic.
  - Executes the same `$vectorSearch` operation Atlas supports.

- **Requirements**:
  - Ensure `vector_index` exists on `default_vector_collection` (check Atlas UI or MongoDB Shell).
  - `embeddingModel.embed()` must match the dimension of your stored embeddings (e.g., 1536 for OpenAI).

